dex\"},{\"operation\":\"PRINT\",\"source\":\"msg[index]\",\"description\":\"printf(%s, msg[index]) - print cookie message to stdout\"}],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"scanf\"]},{\"name\":\"main\",\"address\":\"0x187f\",\"callers\":[\"__libc_start_main\"],\"callees\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"__isoc99_scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"menu_choice\",\"source\":\"scanf(%lld)\",\"type\":\"long long\"}],\"checks\":[\"switch on menu_choice 1-5\"],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"init\",\"menu\",\"scanf\",\"eat_cookie\",\"create_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\",\"exit\"]},{\"name\":\"menu\",\"address\":\"0x17fd\",\"callers\":[\"main\"],\"callees\":[\"puts\",\"__stack_chk_fail\"],\"inputs\":[],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"puts\"]},{\"name\":\"_abort\",\"address\":\"0x11f5\",\"callers\":[\"init\",\"create_cookie\",\"eat_cookie\",\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"callees\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"],\"inputs\":[{\"name\":\"error_msg\",\"source\":\"rdi\"}],\"checks\":[],\"memory_operations\":[],\"calls\":[\"printf\",\"exit\"]}],\"attack_surfaces\":[{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"input\":\"random_byte from /dev/urandom\",\"operation\":\"FREE msg[random_idx] then swap-remove without NULL-out\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"After free, msg[old_cookie_num-1] still contains the freed pointer value (not NULLed). The swap copies msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_idx] but does not clear msg[cookie_num-1]. After cookie_num decrement, the old last slot index == new cookie_num, which is outside the valid range for edit/read checks (idx < cookie_num). However, if the freed pointer is swapped into a still-valid slot (when random_idx != cookie_num-1), the freed pointer becomes accessible via edit_cookie/read_cookie at that index.\"},{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"user-controlled index (scanf %llu)\",\"operation\":\"READ msg[idx] heap pointer, WRITE to heap buffer with msg_size[idx]-1 bytes\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Attacker-controlled index reaches pointer dereference (msg[index]) and size lookup (msg_size[index]). If msg[index] points to freed/reused heap memory, this enables write to freed chunk. Index check is signed jl (index < cookie_num) — negative index not blocked by jl if value is large unsigned, but scanf %llu stores unsigned.\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"input\":\"user-controlled index (scanf %llu)\",\"operation\":\"READ msg[idx] heap pointer, PRINT via printf(%s, msg[idx])\",\"risk\":\"HIGH\",\"reason\":\"Attacker-controlled index reaches pointer dereference and printf output. If msg[index] points to freed/reused heap memory with attacker-controlled content, this enables information leak from heap.\"},{\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"input\":\"user-controlled size (scanf %lld)\",\"operation\":\"ALLOC calloc(size,1), WRITE read(0, buf, size)\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"Size is checked <= 0x100 via signed jle. Since size is read via %lld (signed long long), negative values pass the <= 0x100 check. calloc with negative size (interpreted as very large unsigned) would fail returning NULL, but the code does not check calloc return value before read. If calloc returns NULL, read(0, NULL, size) would crash. No obvious overflow, but the allocated pointer and size are stored in msg/msg_size arrays at cookie_num index.\"},{\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"input\":\"msg_size[index]-1 as read size\",\"operation\":\"READ size from msg_size[index], use as read length\",\"risk\":\"MEDIUM\",\"reason\":\"Read size is derived from msg_size array which is populated during create_cookie and shuffled during eat_cookie. If msg_size and msg arrays become desynchronized after eat_cookie swap-remove, the size used for read may not match the actual buffer at msg[index].\"}],\"facts\":[{\"id\":\"F001\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Binary is PIE, dynamically linked, not stripped, x86-64, compiled with GCC 10.2.0 (Debian 10.2.0-16), source: fortunecookie.c\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F002\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"Full RELRO, NX, Canary, PIE enabled; no FORTIFY\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F003\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"libc is glibc 2.39 (Ubuntu GLIBC 2.39-0ubuntu8.8) at /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6\",\"source\":\"RUNTIME\"},{\"id\":\"F004\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg is a pointer array of 32 elements (8 bytes each) at BSS 0x4060, size 256 bytes\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F005\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size is an int array of 32 elements (4 bytes each) at BSS 0x4160, size 128 bytes\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F006\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg and msg_size are adjacent in BSS: msg[0x4060..0x4160), msg_size[0x4160..0x41e0)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F007\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"cookie_num is at BSS 0x41e8, initialized to 5 by init()\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F008\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"init() calls strdup for 5 fortune strings, stores pointers in msg[0..4] and sizes in msg_size[0..4] (sizes: 0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F009\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie checks cookie_num <= 31 (jle at 0x13bb) and size <= 0x100 (signed jle at 0x13fc), allocates via calloc(size,1), reads via read(0, buf, size), stores in msg[cookie_num] and msg_size[cookie_num]\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F010\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie does NOT check calloc return value before calling read(0, buf, size) — if calloc returns NULL, read writes to address 0\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F011\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie reads 1 byte from /dev/urandom, computes random_idx = byte % cookie_num, frees msg[random_idx], then swaps msg[cookie_num-1] into msg[random_idx] and msg_size[cookie_num-1] into msg_size[random_idx], decrements cookie_num\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F012\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie does NOT NULL out msg[cookie_num-1] after the swap-copy — the old last slot retains the freed pointer value\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F013\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie takes user index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num (signed jl at 0x1684), reads msg_size[index]-1 bytes into msg[index] via read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F014\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"read_cookie takes user index via scanf(%llu), checks index < cookie_num (signed jl at 0x17ad), prints msg[index] via printf(%s, msg[index])\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F015\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie and read_cookie index check uses signed comparison jl (jump if less), comparing 64-bit values in rdx and rax\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F016\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"main loops: calls init, then repeatedly menu+scanf(%lld)+dispatch to eat/create/edit/read/exit\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F017\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"alarm(60) is called in init, setting a 60-second timeout\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F018\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie index is random (from /dev/urandom), not user-controlled\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F019\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"After eat_cookie swap-remove, if random_idx != old cookie_num-1, the freed pointer is now at msg[random_idx] which is still within valid range [0, cookie_num-1)\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F020\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"GOT is in Full RELRO — GOT entries are read-only at runtime (GNU_RELRO segment covers .got)\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F021\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"msg_size elements are 4-byte ints, msg elements are 8-byte pointers; arrays are adjacent with no gap between them\",\"source\":\"ELF\"},{\"id\":\"F022\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"create_cookie size check uses signed jle (cmp rax,0x100; jle) — negative size values pass the check since they are < 0x100 in signed comparison\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"},{\"id\":\"F023\",\"type\":\"FACT\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie/read_cookie index check uses signed jl (cmp rdx,rax; jl) — index read via %llu (unsigned) but compared as signed, so very large unsigned values would be treated as negative and pass the < cookie_num check\",\"source\":\"DISASSEMBLY\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"id\":\"U001\",\"description\":\"Whether the signed jl comparison in edit_cookie/read_cookie allows negative index access\",\"reason\":\"scanf uses %llu (unsigned), but the comparison is jl (signed). If a very large unsigned value is entered (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF), it would be interpreted as -1 in signed context, passing the < cookie_num check. This would cause msg[index] to access memory before msg array (msg_size or earlier BSS). Need S2 to confirm exploitability.\"},{\"id\":\"U002\",\"description\":\"Whether eat_cookie's swap-remove creates a usable UAF primitive\",\"reason\":\"The freed pointer at msg[random_idx] (when random_idx != cookie_num-1) is still accessible via edit_cookie/read_cookie. Whether this constitutes an exploitable UAF depends on S2 analysis of heap state after free and whether the pointer can be reused before access.\"},{\"id\":\"U003\",\"description\":\"Whether msg_size and msg arrays can become desynchronized\",\"reason\":\"eat_cookie swaps both msg and msg_size entries from the last slot. If the freed pointer is at a different index than the last slot, the swap correctly moves both pointer and size. But the old last slot is not cleared, so if cookie_num is later incremented (via create_cookie), the stale pointer at the old index could be overwritten. Need S2 to confirm.\"},{\"id\":\"U004\",\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status cannot be determined from ELF alone\",\"reason\":\"checksec does not report CET flags. Need runtime check via /proc/cpuinfo or arch_prctl.\"},{\"id\":\"U005\",\"description\":\"Whether create_cookie with negative/zero size leads to exploitable behavior\",\"reason\":\"calloc(negative_size, 1) would interpret negative as very large unsigned, likely returning NULL. Code does not check calloc return, so read(0, NULL, size) would crash (SIGSEGV). Whether this can be leveraged depends on S2 analysis.\"}],\"raw\":{\"elf\":\"ELF64 LSB PIE, x86-64, dynamically linked, interpreter /lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2, not stripped, BuildID 84dab319bf6fe22134cf0338cbd8071fd8bc06c2, GCC 10.2.0 (Debian 10.2.0-16), source: fortunecookie.c\",\"sections\":\"29 sections; .text@0x1110(0x891,AX); .rodata@0x2000(0x266,A); .data@0x4000(0x10,WA); .bss@0x4020(0x1d0,WA); .got@0x3f58(0xa8,WA); .plt@0x1020(0xe0,AX); .init_array@0x3d58(0x8,WA); .fini_array@0x3d60(0x8,WA)\",\"symbols\":\"Key: main@0x187f, init@0x1232, create_cookie@0x1399, eat_cookie@0x14e1, edit_cookie@0x1628, read_cookie@0x1751, menu@0x17fd, _abort@0x11f5; Globals: msg@0x4060(256B), msg_size@0x4160(128B), cookie_num@0x41e8(8B), urandom@0x41e0(8B), stdout@0x4020, stdin@0x4030, stderr@0x4040\",\"disassembly\":\"eat_cookie: fread 1 byte from urandom, idx=byte%cookie_num, free(msg[idx]), swap msg[cookie_num-1]->msg[idx], swap msg_size[cookie_num-1]->msg_size[idx], cookie_num--, NO NULL-OUT of old last slot. edit_cookie: scanf(%llu) idx, check idx<cookie_num(jl at 0x1684), read(0,msg[idx],msg_size[idx]-1). read_cookie: scanf(%llu) idx, check idx<cookie_num(jl at 0x17ad), printf(%s,msg[idx]). create_cookie: scanf(%lld) size, check size<=0x100(signed jle at 0x13fc), calloc(size,1) with NO NULL check, read(0,buf,size), store in msg[cookie_num]/msg_size[cookie_num], cookie_num++. main: init->loop{menu,scanf(%lld),switch 1-5 dispatch}. init: setvbuf stdin/stdout/stderr, alarm(60), fopen(/dev/urandom), strdup 5 fortune strings into msg[0..4], msg_size[0..4]={0x50,0x30,0x18,0x38,0x40}, cookie_num=5.\"}},\"vulnerability_report\":{\"schema\":\"VulnerabilityReport\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"summary\":{\"total_bugs\":3,\"high_severity\":2,\"medium_severity\":1,\"low_severity\":0},\"vulnerabilities\":[{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"title\":\"OOB_SIGNEDNESS_MISMATCH_IN_INDEX_VALIDATION\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Signedness Error\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie 和 read_cookie 通过 scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") 读取用户索引（unsigned long long），但边界检查使用 jl（有符号比较指令）。当输入一个大无符号值（如 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF，即有符号 -1）时，该值在有符号比较中为负数，满足 index < cookie_num 条件，从而绕过边界检查。随后该值被直接用于计算 msg[index] 和 msg_size[index] 的内存偏移（lea rdx, [rax*8+0x0] 和 lea rdx, [rax*4+0x0]），导致访问 msg 数组之前的 BSS 内存区域。负索引 -4 可访问 stderr FILE 指针（0x4040），-6 可访问 stdin（0x4030），-8 可访问 stdout（0x4020）。\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"read_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg\",\"msg_size\",\"stdout\",\"stdin\",\"stderr\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"cookie_index via scanf(\\\"%llu\\\")\",\"entry_function\":\"main\",\"data_flow\":[\"main 读取菜单选项 scanf(\\\"%lld\\\")，分发到 edit_cookie(选项3) 或 read_cookie(选项4)\",\"edit_cookie/read_cookie 调用 scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") 读取用户索引到栈变量 [rbp-0x10]\",\"索引值与 cookie_num 比较：cmp rdx, rax; jl（有符号小于跳转）\",\"大无符号值（如 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF）在有符号比较中被视为 -1，-1 < cookie_num 为真，通过检查\",\"通过检查后，索引被用于计算 msg[index] 地址：lea rdx,[rax*8+0]; lea rax,[rip+msg]; mov rax,[rdx+rax] —— 负索引访问 msg 数组之前的 BSS 内存\",\"edit_cookie: read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) —— 向负索引处的指针写入数据\",\"read_cookie: printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[index]) —— 将负索引处的指针解引用并打印为字符串\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"索引应为无符号比较（jb/jae），确保只允许 0 <= index < cookie_num 范围内的值\",\"actual\":\"使用 jl（jump if less, signed）比较 64 位索引与 cookie_num，允许负值通过检查\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"缺少无符号比较（应使用 jb 而非 jl），且缺少下界检查（index >= 0）\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"OOB array access via negative index\",\"address\":\"0x1684 (edit_cookie jl), 0x17ad (read_cookie jl), 0x16c3-16d2 (edit_cookie msg[index] deref), 0x17bf-17ce (read_cookie msg[index] deref)\",\"expression\":\"msg[index] where index is attacker-controlled and bypasses signed jl check via large unsigned value\",\"target\":\"BSS globals before msg array: stdout(0x4020), stdin(0x4030), stderr(0x4040) FILE pointers\",\"size\":\"8 bytes per pointer dereference (msg[index]), 4 bytes per int read (msg_size[index])\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"OOB_READ\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie 中 printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[index]) 使用负索引解引用 BSS 中的 FILE 指针（如 stdout/stdin/stderr），将 FILE 结构体内容作为字符串打印到 stdout，可能泄露 libc/堆地址信息。Preconditions: 输入大无符号值（如 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC 对应 -4）作为索引。\"},{\"type\":\"OOB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie 中 read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) 使用负索引，将数据写入 msg[index] 解引用的地址。当 index=-4 时，msg[-4] = stderr FILE 指针，read 向 FILE 结构体写入用户数据，导致内存破坏。写入大小由 msg_size[index]-1 决定，msg_size[-4] 读取 msg[30] 的低4字节。Preconditions: 输入大无符号值作为索引，且 msg_size 对应位置有合适的值。\"},{\"type\":\"INFO_LEAK\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie 使用 printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[-4]) 打印 stderr FILE 指针指向的 FILE 结构体内容，可能泄露 libc 内部地址。Preconditions: 输入 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC 作为索引。\"},{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie 向 FILE 结构体写入用户控制的数据，破坏 FILE 结构体内部状态。Preconditions: 输入对应负索引的大无符号值。\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E001\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1671\",\"description\":\"scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") 读取无符号 long long 索引到 [rbp-0x10]\"},{\"id\":\"E002\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681-0x1684\",\"description\":\"cmp rdx, rax; jl 0x1692 —— 使用有符号比较 jl（jump if less）检查 index < cookie_num，大无符号值被视为负数通过检查\"},{\"id\":\"E003\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16c3-0x16d2\",\"description\":\"lea rcx,[rax*8+0]; lea rax,[rip+msg]; mov rax,[rcx+rax] —— 使用通过检查的负索引计算 msg[index] 地址并解引用，访问 msg 数组之前的 BSS 内存\"},{\"id\":\"E004\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17aa-0x17ad\",\"description\":\"cmp rdx, rax; jl 0x17bb —— 同样的有符号比较 jl 检查，同样的 signedness mismatch\"},{\"id\":\"E005\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17bf-0x17ce\",\"description\":\"lea rdx,[rax*8+0]; lea rax,[rip+msg]; mov rax,[rdx+rax] —— 使用负索引解引用 msg[index]，获取 BSS 中的 FILE 指针\"},{\"id\":\"E006\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17d2-0x17e1\",\"description\":\"printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[index]) —— 将负索引获取的 FILE 指针解引用并打印为字符串，可能导致信息泄露\"},{\"id\":\"E007\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie/read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x4060\",\"description\":\"msg 数组位于 BSS 0x4060，负索引 -4 访问 0x4040（stderr FILE*），-6 访问 0x4030（stdin FILE*），-8 访问 0x4020（stdout FILE*）。这些 FILE 指针在 init() 中通过 setvbuf 初始化，指向 libc 中的 FILE 结构体。\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"动态验证输入 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC 作为 read_cookie 索引时，printf 是否输出 FILE 结构体内容\",\"动态验证输入对应负索引作为 edit_cookie 索引时，read 是否向 FILE 结构体写入数据\",\"确认 glibc 2.39 下 FILE 结构体的内存布局和可泄露信息范围\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-002\",\"title\":\"INTEGER_UNDERFLOW_IN_EDIT_COOKIE_SIZE_CALCULATION\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Integer Underflow\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie 计算 read 的长度参数为 msg_size[index]-1。msg_size 元素为 4 字节 int。当 msg_size[index] = 0 时（可通过 create_cookie(size=0) 创建），0 - 1 在 32 位运算中结果为 0xFFFFFFFF。随后 movsxd rdx, eax 将其符号扩展为 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF（64 位），作为 read() 的 count 参数（size_t 无符号）。read() 尝试向堆缓冲区写入最多 2^64-1 字节，导致堆缓冲区溢出。\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"edit_cookie\",\"create_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg_size\",\"msg\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"message_size via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") in create_cookie; new_message via read() in edit_cookie\",\"entry_function\":\"main\",\"data_flow\":[\"main 分发到 create_cookie（选项2）\",\"create_cookie: scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") 读取 size=0，0 <= 0x100 通过 signed jle 检查\",\"calloc(0, 1) 返回有效堆指针（glibc 行为，分配最小 chunk）\",\"read(0, buf, 0) 读取 0 字节\",\"msg[cookie_num] = buf, msg_size[cookie_num] = 0, cookie_num++\",\"用户选择选项3 进入 edit_cookie\",\"edit_cookie: scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") 读取索引（指向 msg_size=0 的 cookie）\",\"msg_size[index] = 0, 计算 msg_size[index] - 1 = 0xFFFFFFFF（32 位下溢）\",\"movsxd rdx, eax -> rdx = 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF（符号扩展为 64 位）\",\"read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) -> 堆缓冲区溢出\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"在计算 msg_size[index]-1 前应检查 msg_size[index] > 0，或使用无符号运算避免下溢\",\"actual\":\"直接执行 sub eax, 0x1 无任何下界检查，msg_size[index]=0 时产生整数下溢\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"缺少 msg_size[index] > 0 的前置验证；缺少对 read count 参数的合理性检查\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"Heap buffer overflow via integer underflow in read size\",\"address\":\"0x16b9 (sub eax, 0x1), 0x16bc (movsxd rdx, eax), 0x16de (call read@plt)\",\"expression\":\"read(0, msg[index], (size_t)(int)(msg_size[index] - 1)) where msg_size[index]=0\",\"target\":\"heap buffer pointed to by msg[index] (from calloc(0,1), minimal allocation)\",\"size\":\"up to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF bytes (limited by available stdin data and memory mappings)\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"MEMORY_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"read() 向 calloc(0,1) 分配的最小堆 chunk 写入超过其分配大小的数据，破坏堆元数据和相邻堆对象。Preconditions: 先用 create_cookie(size=0) 创建 msg_size=0 的 cookie，再用 edit_cookie 编辑该 cookie。\"},{\"type\":\"DATA_CORRUPTION\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"堆溢出可能覆盖相邻堆 chunk 的数据，破坏其他 cookie 消息内容或堆管理结构。Preconditions: 同上。\"},{\"type\":\"CRASH\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"当溢出写入到达未映射内存页时触发 SIGSEGV。Preconditions: 同上，且写入数据量足够大。\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E008\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13f6-0x13fc\",\"description\":\"cmp rax, 0x100; jle —— size=0 通过 signed jle 检查（0 <= 0x100）\"},{\"id\":\"E009\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1416-0x141b\",\"description\":\"call calloc@plt; mov [rbp-0x10], rax —— calloc(0, 1) 返回值存入 buf，无 NULL 检查（glibc calloc(0,1) 返回有效指针）\"},{\"id\":\"E010\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1498-0x14a9\",\"description\":\"mov ecx, edx; mov [rdx+rax], ecx —— msg_size[cookie_num] = (int)size = 0，存入 0 值\"},{\"id\":\"E011\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16b6-0x16b9\",\"description\":\"mov eax, [rdx+rax]; sub eax, 0x1 —— 读取 msg_size[index]=0，减1得到 0xFFFFFFFF（32位整数下溢）\"},{\"id\":\"E012\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16bc\",\"description\":\"movsxd rdx, eax —— 将 0xFFFFFFFF 符号扩展为 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF，作为 read() 的 count 参数\"},{\"id\":\"E013\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"call read@plt —— read(0, msg[index], 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)，向最小堆 chunk 写入近乎无限数据\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"动态验证 create_cookie(size=0) 后 calloc(0,1) 返回非 NULL 指针\",\"动态验证 edit_cookie 对 msg_size=0 的 cookie 执行时 read 的实际写入行为\",\"确认 glibc 2.39 下 calloc(0,1) 的分配大小和堆布局\"]},{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-003\",\"title\":\"MISSING_CALLOC_NULL_CHECK_IN_CREATE_COOKIE\",\"root_cause\":{\"type\":\"Improper Input Validation\",\"description\":\"create_cookie 通过 scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") 读取 size，使用 signed jle 检查 size <= 0x100。负值（如 -1）通过检查后，calloc(0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, 1) 因请求过大分配返回 NULL。代码未检查 calloc 返回值即调用 read(0, NULL, size)，导致向地址 0 写入数据。\"},\"affected_functions\":[\"create_cookie\"],\"affected_objects\":[\"msg\"],\"attack_surface\":{\"input\":\"message_size via scanf(\\\"%lld\\\")\",\"entry_function\":\"main\",\"data_flow\":[\"main 分发到 create_cookie（选项2）\",\"scanf(\\\"%lld\\\") 读取 size = -1（0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF）\",\"cmp rax, 0x100; jle —— -1 <= 0x100 有符号比较为真，通过检查\",\"calloc(0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, 1) —— nmemb 被解释为 size_t（无符号），值为 2^64-1，分配失败返回 NULL\",\"read(0, NULL, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF) —— 向地址 0 写入，NULL 指针解引用\"]},\"security_check\":{\"expected\":\"应检查 calloc 返回值是否为 NULL，且应使用无符号比较或拒绝负 size 值\",\"actual\":\"signed jle 允许负 size 通过；calloc 返回值未检查直接用于 read\",\"missing_or_incorrect\":\"缺少 calloc 返回值 NULL 检查；size 检查使用有符号比较允许负值\"},\"vulnerable_operation\":{\"operation\":\"NULL pointer dereference via unchecked calloc return\",\"address\":\"0x1416 (call calloc), 0x1437-0x1443 (read with NULL buf)\",\"expression\":\"read(0, calloc(negative_size, 1), negative_size) where calloc returns NULL\",\"target\":\"address 0 (NULL)\",\"size\":\"up to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF bytes (read count = negative size as unsigned)\"},\"impact\":[{\"type\":\"NULL_POINTER_DEREF\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"calloc 返回 NULL 后，read(0, NULL, size) 尝试向地址 0 写入数据，触发 SIGSEGV。Preconditions: 输入负值作为 message size（如 -1）。\"},{\"type\":\"CRASH\",\"status\":\"CANDIDATE\",\"reason\":\"NULL 指针解引用导致进程崩溃（SIGSEGV），可用作拒绝服务。Preconditions: 输入负值作为 message size。\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E014\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x13f6-0x13fc\",\"description\":\"cmp rax, 0x100; jle —— signed jle 检查允许负 size 值通过（-1 <= 0x100 为真）\"},{\"id\":\"E015\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1416-0x141b\",\"description\":\"call calloc@plt; mov [rbp-0x10], rax —— calloc 返回值直接存入 buf，无 test rax,rax / je NULL 检查\"},{\"id\":\"E016\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"create_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1437-0x1443\",\"description\":\"mov rax, [rbp-0x10]; mov rsi, rax; call read@plt —— 将 calloc 返回值（可能为 NULL）直接作为 read 的 buf 参数\"}],\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"verification_required\":[\"动态验证输入 -1 作为 size 时 calloc 是否返回 NULL\",\"动态验证 read(0, NULL, ...) 是否触发 SIGSEGV\",\"确认 glibc 2.39 下 calloc(huge_value, 1) 的确切行为\"]}],\"non_vulnerabilities\":[{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie 的 swap-remove 操作不会创建可直接访问的 UAF\",\"reason\":\"free(msg[random_idx]) 后，swap 将 msg[cookie_num-1]（有效指针）复制到 msg[random_idx]，覆盖了 freed 指针。旧最后槽位 msg[old_cookie_num-1] 未清零，但该索引在 cookie_num-- 后等于新的 cookie_num，不满足 index < cookie_num 检查，无法通过 edit_cookie/read_cookie 访问。虽然存在指针重复（同一指针在两个位置），但重复副本始终位于不可访问的索引（>= cookie_num）。当 create_cookie 增加 cookie_num 时，旧槽位会被新分配覆盖。因此不构成可直接触发的 UAF。\"},{\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"description\":\"read_cookie 的 printf 使用固定格式字符串 \\\"%s\\\\n\\\\n\\\"，非格式字符串漏洞\",\"reason\":\"反汇编显示 read_cookie 在 0x17d5 加载格式字符串地址 0x21a9（\\\"%s\\\\n\\\\n\\\"），在 0x17e1 调用 printf。用户输入的 cookie 消息作为第二个参数（rsi）传入，不是格式字符串本身。不存在格式字符串漏洞。\"},{\"function\":\"eat_cookie\",\"description\":\"eat_cookie 的 random_idx 来自 /dev/urandom，非攻击者可控\",\"reason\":\"fread 从 urandom 读取 1 字节，random_idx = byte % cookie_num。虽然攻击者无法控制具体索引，但 eat_cookie 的 swap-remove 逻辑本身不构成漏洞（见 non_vulnerabilities 第一条）。\"}],\"unresolved\":[{\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) 状态无法从 ELF 确定\",\"reason\":\"checksec 不报告 CET 标志，需要运行时检查 /proc/cpuinfo 或 arch_prctl\",\"required_next_step\":\"S3/S4 阶段在运行时确认 CET 是否启用，以评估对控制流劫持的限制\"},{\"description\":\"负索引 OOB 访问的具体可利用性取决于 FILE 结构体布局\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie 通过负索引访问 stdout/stdin/stderr FILE 指针并 printf(\\\"%s\\\") 打印，具体能泄露哪些地址取决于 glibc 2.39 的 FILE 结构体内部布局\",\"required_next_step\":\"S3 动态验证 printf(\\\"%s\\\", stdout_ptr) 实际输出的内容和泄露的地址范围\"},{\"description\":\"堆溢出的实际破坏范围取决于堆布局\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie 的整数下溢导致 read 向 calloc(0,1) 的最小 chunk 写入，实际能覆盖哪些相邻堆对象取决于当时的堆状态\",\"required_next_step\":\"S3 动态验证堆布局，确认溢出能覆盖的目标对象\"}]},\"primitive_reports\":[{\"schema\":\"PrimitiveReport\",\"version\":\"1.0\",\"stage\":\"S3\",\"target_bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"summary\":{\"analyzed_bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"total_primitives\":3,\"verified\":2,\"theoretical\":1,\"candidate\":0,\"unknown\":0},\"primitives\":[{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-001\",\"type\":\"INFO_LEAK\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"kind\":\"DIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Signedness mismatch in index validation: scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") reads unsigned long long index, but boundary check uses jl (signed less-than). Large unsigned values (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFC = -4 signed) pass the check as negative < cookie_num.\",\"description\":\"read_cookie uses printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[index]) with negative index to dereference FILE pointers (stderr/stdin/stdout) in BSS, printing FILE structure content to stdout.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001\",\"Signedness mismatch: scanf %llu + jl signed comparison\",\"Negative index bypasses boundary check\",\"msg[-4] = *(0x4040) = stderr FILE* pointer to libc _IO_2_1_stderr_\",\"printf(\\\"%s\\\", msg[-4]) prints FILE struct content until null byte\",\"INFO_LEAK: FILE _flags field (0xfbad2087) leaked\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"Array index (negative via unsigned overflow)\",\"how\":\"scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") reads large unsigned value (e.g. 18446744073709551612 = -4 signed), passes jl check\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"Input large unsigned value (e.g. 18446744073709551612 for index -4) as cookie index in read_cookie\",\"necessity\":\"Required to bypass signed jl boundary check and access negative index\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-02\",\"description\":\"FILE pointers (stderr/stdin/stdout) must be initialized in BSS before msg array\",\"necessity\":\"Required: negative index must hit a valid (non-NULL) pointer to dereference and print\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-03\",\"description\":\"FILE structure must have non-null bytes at start (flags field) for printf to output\",\"necessity\":\"Required: printf %s stops at null byte; _flags field 0xfbad2087 has byte 5 = 0x00, limiting leak to 4 bytes\",\"verified\":true}],\"alias_key_findings\":[{\"expression\":\"msg[-4] = *(0x4060 + (-4)*8) = *(0x4040)\",\"alias\":\"stderr FILE* pointer in BSS\",\"implication\":\"Negative index -4 aliases stderr FILE pointer, dereferencing it gives libc FILE structure address\"},{\"expression\":\"msg[-6] = *(0x4030) = stdin FILE*\",\"alias\":\"stdin FILE* pointer in BSS\",\"implication\":\"Index -6 aliases stdin FILE pointer\"},{\"expression\":\"msg[-8] = *(0x4020) = stdout FILE*\",\"alias\":\"stdout FILE* pointer in BSS\",\"implication\":\"Index -8 aliases stdout FILE pointer\"}],\"verification_plan\":{\"method\":\"Run read_cookie with index 18446744073709551612 (-4 signed), observe leaked FILE structure bytes in output\",\"environment\":\"Linux x86-64, glibc 2.39, PIE binary\",\"run_command\":\"cd /work/test && python3 poc-BUG-001.py\",\"expected_evidence\":[\"Leaked bytes 87 20 ad fb (stderr _flags = 0xfbad2087)\",\"4 bytes leaked before null terminator at byte 5\"]},\"mitigations\":[{\"name\":\"PIE\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"PIE randomizes binary base address, but FILE pointers in BSS are always at fixed offset from msg array. The negative index still works regardless of PIE.\"},{\"name\":\"Full RELRO\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on INFO_LEAK primitive - this reads FILE structure content, not GOT.\"},{\"name\":\"NX\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on INFO_LEAK primitive.\"},{\"name\":\"Canary\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on INFO_LEAK primitive - no stack overflow involved.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E001\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17bb-0x17e1\",\"description\":\"GDB: read_cookie with index -4, rsi=0x7ffff7fa74e0 (_IO_2_1_stderr_), printf prints 4 bytes: 87 20 ad fb = _flags field 0xfbad2087. FILE struct at +8 contains libc pointer 0x00007ffff7fa7563 but null byte at offset 4 stops printf.\"},{\"id\":\"E002\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17ad\",\"description\":\"GDB: cmp rdx,rax; jl - rdx=0xfffffffffffffffc (-4), rax=5 (cookie_num). -4 < 5 signed = true, check bypassed.\"},{\"id\":\"E003\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"read_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x17bf-0x17ce\",\"description\":\"lea rdx,[rax*8+0]; lea rax,[rip+msg]; mov rax,[rdx+rax] - negative index computes address before msg array, accessing BSS FILE pointers\"}],\"verification_result\":{\"executed\":true,\"poc_path\":\"/work/test/poc-BUG-001.py\",\"written_value\":\"\",\"read_value\":\"0xfbad2087\",\"fault_address\":\"\",\"return_code\":0,\"details\":\"PoC output: Leaked bytes (hex): 8720adfb, FILE _flags = 0xfbad2087. GDB confirmed rsi=0x7ffff7fa74e0 (_IO_2_1_stderr_), printf outputs 4 bytes of FILE _flags before null at byte 5.\"},\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"notes\":\"INFO_LEAK leaks 4 bytes of FILE _flags field (0xfbad2087 for stderr). The leak is limited to 4 bytes because byte 5 of _flags is 0x00. While this specific leak is only the flags value (not a direct libc pointer), it proves the OOB read primitive works. The FILE structure at offset +8 contains libc pointers (0x00007ffff7fa7563) but they cannot be reached via printf %s due to the null byte. This is classified as INFO_LEAK (not ARB_READ) because the read target is limited to fixed FILE pointers at fixed negative indices, not attacker-controlled addresses.\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-002\",\"type\":\"RELATIVE_WRITE\",\"status\":\"VERIFIED\",\"kind\":\"DIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Signedness mismatch in index validation: scanf(\\\"%llu\\\") reads unsigned long long index, but boundary check uses jl (signed less-than). Large unsigned values pass the check as negative.\",\"description\":\"edit_cookie uses read(0, msg[index], msg_size[index]-1) with negative index -11 to write to __dso_handle (self-referencing pointer at .data 0x4008). msg_size[-11] aliases high 4 bytes of msg[26], which is 0x00005555 (small positive) when msg[26] is filled with a heap pointer.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001\",\"Signedness mismatch: scanf %llu + jl signed comparison\",\"Negative index -11 bypasses boundary check\",\"msg[-11] = *(0x4008) = __dso_handle (self-referencing: *(&X)==&X)\",\"msg_size[-11] = *(0x4134) = high 4 bytes of msg[26] = 0x00005555 (small positive)\",\"read(0, __dso_handle, 0x5554) writes user data to __dso_handle address\",\"RELATIVE_WRITE: write to fixed .data address (__dso_handle)\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"Write data (content) and write occurs at fixed target (__dso_handle address)\",\"how\":\"edit_cookie with index -11: read(0, msg[-11], msg_size[-11]-1) writes to __dso_handle. Content is attacker-controlled via stdin. Target is fixed (__dso_handle at .data 0x4008).\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"Input large unsigned value 18446744073709551605 (-11 signed) as cookie index in edit_cookie\",\"necessity\":\"Required to bypass signed jl boundary check and access negative index -11\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-02\",\"description\":\"Create 22 filler cookies (indices 5-26) to fill msg[26] with a heap pointer, making msg_size[-11] = high 4 bytes = 0x00005555 (small positive)\",\"necessity\":\"Required: without filling msg[26], msg_size[-11]=0, causing integer underflow to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF which makes read() fail (returns -1). With msg[26] filled, msg_size[-11]=0x5555, giving msg_size[-11]-1=0x5554 (21844), a valid small positive size.\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-03\",\"description\":\"__dso_handle must be self-referencing (*(&X)==&X) and located at .data 0x4008\",\"necessity\":\"Required: msg[-11] must be a valid writable pointer. __dso_handle is self-referencing (GDB verified: val=0x555555558008, addr=0x555555558008), pointing to writable .data segment.\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-04\",\"description\":\"Write size (msg_size[-11]-1 = 0x5554 = 21844) must be small enough that buf+size stays within writable memory\",\"necessity\":\"Required: if size is too large (e.g. 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF when msg_size=0, or ~1.4GB when aliasing heap pointer low bytes), read() fails because buf+count exceeds address space. Size 0x5554 keeps write within .data segment.\",\"verified\":true}],\"alias_key_findings\":[{\"expression\":\"msg[-11] = *(0x4060 + (-11)*8) = *(0x4008) = __dso_handle\",\"alias\":\"__dso_handle self-referencing pointer at .data 0x4008\",\"implication\":\"Write target is __dso_handle address (fixed .data address). Since __dso_handle is self-referencing, writing to *(__dso_handle) modifies __dso_handle itself.\"},{\"expression\":\"msg_size[-11] = *(0x4160 + (-11)*4) = *(0x4134) = high 4 bytes of msg[26]\",\"alias\":\"High 4 bytes of msg[26] heap pointer\",\"implication\":\"When msg[26] is filled with heap pointer 0x0000555555559xxx, high 4 bytes = 0x00005555 = 21845 (small positive). This is the GOLDEN alias: size field aliases pointer high half, giving valid small positive size. msg_size[-11]-1 = 0x5554 = 21844.\"},{\"expression\":\"msg_size[-4] = *(0x4150) = low 4 bytes of msg[30]\",\"alias\":\"Low 4 bytes of msg[30] heap pointer\",\"implication\":\"When msg[30] is filled, low 4 bytes = ~0x55559000 (large). msg_size[-4]-1 is too large, read() fails. This is the DEAD END alias: size aliases pointer low half, giving large value.\"},{\"expression\":\"msg_size[-3] = *(0x4154) = high 4 bytes of msg[30]\",\"alias\":\"High 4 bytes of msg[30] heap pointer\",\"implication\":\"When msg[30] is filled, high 4 bytes = 0x00005555 (small positive). But msg[-3] = *(0x4048) = completed.0 = 0 (NULL). Dead: pointer is NULL even though size is valid.\"}],\"verification_plan\":{\"method\":\"1. Create 22 filler cookies (size=8 each) to fill msg[5..26]. 2. edit_cookie with index -11, send 8 bytes of data. 3. GDB verify __dso_handle changed from 0x555555558008 to overwritten value. 4. Observe SIGSEGV at post-write check (proves write occurred).\",\"environment\":\"Linux x86-64, glibc 2.39, PIE binary\",\"run_command\":\"cd /work/test && python3 poc-BUG-001.py\",\"expected_evidence\":[\"GDB: __dso_handle before = 0x555555558008 (self-referencing)\",\"GDB: __dso_handle after = 0x4141414141414141 (overwritten with AAAAAAAA)\",\"GDB: read return = 0xb (11 bytes written)\",\"GDB: msg_size[-11]-1 = 0x5554 (21844, valid size)\",\"Process exit code: -11 (SIGSEGV at post-write check)\"]},\"mitigations\":[{\"name\":\"PIE\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"PIE randomizes base address, but __dso_handle is at fixed offset from msg array. The negative index -11 always reaches __dso_handle regardless of PIE base. However, the written value (if used for two-step write) must be a valid runtime address, requiring PIE base knowledge.\"},{\"name\":\"Full RELRO\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"Full RELRO makes GOT read-only, but this primitive writes to .data segment (__dso_handle), not GOT. No impact on this primitive.\"},{\"name\":\"NX\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on RELATIVE_WRITE primitive.\"},{\"name\":\"Canary\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact - no stack overflow involved. The write targets .data segment, not stack.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E004\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"GDB: Before read call: rsi=0x555555558008 (__dso_handle, write target), rdx=0x5554 (msg_size[-11]-1 = 21844, valid size). msg[26]=0x555555559870 (filled), msg_size[-11]=0x5555 (high 4 bytes of msg[26]).\"},{\"id\":\"E005\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16e3\",\"description\":\"GDB: After read call: __dso_handle changed from 0x555555558008 to 0x4141414141414141 (overwritten with 'AAAAAAAA'). read return (rax) = 0xb (11 bytes written). Write succeeded.\"},{\"id\":\"E006\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1705\",\"description\":\"GDB: SIGSEGV at edit_cookie+0xdd (0x1705): movzx eax, [rax] where rax = msg[-11] (re-read as 0x4141414141414141) + read_return (0xb) = 0x414141414141414c. Invalid address -> crash. Proves msg[-11] was overwritten.\"},{\"id\":\"E007\",\"type\":\"STATIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x1681-0x1684\",\"description\":\"cmp rdx,rax; jl 0x1692 - signed comparison allows index -11 (0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF5) to pass as -11 < cookie_num\"}],\"verification_result\":{\"executed\":true,\"poc_path\":\"/work/test/poc-BUG-001.py\",\"written_value\":\"0x4141414141414141\",\"read_value\":\"\",\"fault_address\":\"0x414141414141414c\",\"return_code\":-11,\"details\":\"GDB verified: __dso_handle at 0x555555558008 changed from 0x555555558008 (self-referencing) to 0x4141414141414141 (overwritten with AAAAAAAA). read(0, 0x555555558008, 0x5554) returned 0xb (11 bytes). SIGSEGV at edit_cookie+0xdd (0x1705) when re-reading overwritten msg[-11] and dereferencing at 0x414141414141414c. PoC exit code: -11 (SIGSEGV).\"},\"confidence\":\"HIGH\",\"notes\":\"RELATIVE_WRITE (not ARB_WRITE) because the write target is a FIXED address (__dso_handle at .data 0x4008), not attacker-controlled. The write content is attacker-controlled. The write size (21844) is derived from msg[26] high 4 bytes, which is a side effect of heap allocation layout. The post-write crash occurs because edit_cookie re-reads msg[index] (now overwritten) and dereferences it. This crash is a side effect, not the primitive itself - the write already succeeded before the crash.\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"PRIM-003\",\"type\":\"ARB_WRITE\",\"status\":\"THEORETICAL\",\"kind\":\"INDIRECT\",\"source\":{\"bug_id\":\"BUG-001\",\"root_cause\":\"Same signedness mismatch as PRIM-002. The two-step write leverages the self-referencing nature of __dso_handle to upgrade RELATIVE_WRITE to ARB_WRITE.\",\"description\":\"Two-step write: Step 1 overwrites __dso_handle (self-referencing pointer) with target address Y. Step 2 uses same index -11, but now msg[-11]=Y, so read(0, Y, size) writes to attacker-controlled Y.\"},\"chain\":[\"BUG-001\",\"Signedness mismatch allows negative index -11\",\"msg[-11] = __dso_handle (self-referencing: *(&X)==&X)\",\"Step 1: edit_cookie(-11, Y) -> read(0, &__dso_handle, 0x5554) overwrites __dso_handle with Y\",\"Step 2: edit_cookie(-11, payload) -> msg[-11] now = Y, read(0, Y, 0x5554) writes payload to Y\",\"ARB_WRITE: attacker controls both WHAT (payload) and WHERE (Y)\"],\"controlled_element\":{\"what\":\"Both write target address (Y) and write content (payload)\",\"how\":\"Step 1: write target address Y to __dso_handle via edit_cookie(-11, Y). Step 2: write payload to *Y via edit_cookie(-11, payload). Same index, different data.\",\"reach_sensitive_operation\":true},\"preconditions\":[{\"id\":\"PC-01\",\"description\":\"All preconditions from PRIM-002 (fill msg[26], use index -11, __dso_handle self-referencing)\",\"necessity\":\"Required: same setup as PRIM-002\",\"verified\":true},{\"id\":\"PC-02\",\"description\":\"Step 1 must not crash: Y + read_return_value must be a readable address\",\"necessity\":\"Required: after Step 1 write, edit_cookie re-reads msg[-11] (=Y) and dereferences Y+read_return. If Y points to readable memory, no crash and program returns to menu for Step 2.\",\"verified\":false},{\"id\":\"PC-03\",\"description\":\"Attacker must know PIE base to construct valid target address Y\",\"necessity\":\"Required: Y must be a valid writable address in process memory. With PIE, addresses are randomized. Attacker needs PIE base leak (e.g. from PRIM-001 or other source) to construct Y.\",\"verified\":false},{\"id\":\"PC-04\",\"description\":\"msg_size[-11] must remain 0x5555 after Step 1 (msg[26] unchanged by write to __dso_handle)\",\"necessity\":\"Required: Step 2 uses same msg_size[-11]-1 = 0x5554 as write size. Since __dso_handle is at .data 0x4008 and msg[26] is at BSS 0x4130, writing to __dso_handle does not affect msg[26].\",\"verified\":true}],\"alias_key_findings\":[{\"expression\":\"__dso_handle: *(&X) == &X where X = __dso_handle at 0x4008\",\"alias\":\"Self-referencing pointer\",\"implication\":\"Writing to *(__dso_handle) modifies __dso_handle itself. This is the key enabler for two-step write: Step 1 changes the pointer, Step 2 writes through the changed pointer.\"},{\"expression\":\"msg[-11] = __dso_handle (re-read each time edit_cookie is called)\",\"alias\":\"msg[-11] always reads current __dso_handle value\",\"implication\":\"After Step 1 overwrites __dso_handle with Y, Step 2's msg[-11] = Y. The same index gives different write targets across two calls.\"}],\"verification_plan\":{\"method\":\"1. Create 22 filler cookies. 2. Step 1: edit_cookie(-11, Y) where Y is a valid readable+writable address (e.g. BSS address). 3. Verify no crash (Y+read_return is readable). 4. Step 2: edit_cookie(-11, payload). 5. GDB verify payload written at Y.\",\"environment\":\"Linux x86-64, glibc 2.39, PIE binary. Requires PIE base leak for Y construction.\",\"run_command\":\"cd /work/test && python3 poc-BUG-001.py\",\"expected_evidence\":[\"Step 1: __dso_handle overwritten with Y, no crash\",\"Step 2: payload written at address Y (GDB verified)\",\"Two different Y values tested to prove address controllability\"]},\"mitigations\":[{\"name\":\"PIE\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"PIE randomizes all addresses. To construct valid Y for two-step write, attacker needs PIE base. PRIM-001 leaks FILE _flags (not a direct address), so additional leak may be needed. This is the main barrier to full ARB_WRITE verification.\"},{\"name\":\"Full RELRO\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on two-step write - writes target .data/BSS, not GOT.\"},{\"name\":\"NX\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact on ARB_WRITE primitive.\"},{\"name\":\"Canary\",\"present\":true,\"primitive_impact\":\"No impact - no stack overflow involved.\"}],\"evidence\":[{\"id\":\"E008\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16de\",\"description\":\"GDB (from PRIM-002): read(0, 0x555555558008, 0x5554) successfully wrote 0x4141414141414141 to __dso_handle. This proves Step 1 of two-step write works: the write target (__dso_handle) can be overwritten with arbitrary data.\"},{\"id\":\"E009\",\"type\":\"DYNAMIC\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"0x16f9\",\"description\":\"GDB (from PRIM-002 crash): After write, msg[-11] is re-read as 0x4141414141414141 (overwritten value), proving that msg[-11] reflects the current __dso_handle value. This confirms Step 2 would use the overwritten value as write target.\"},{\"id\":\"E010\",\"type\":\"DERIVED\",\"function\":\"edit_cookie\",\"address\":\"\",\"description\":\"Structural derivation: Since __dso_handle is self-referencing (*(&X)==&X) and msg[-11] always reads current __dso_handle value, two sequential edit_cookie(-11) calls with different data achieve: Call 1 sets msg[-11]=Y, Call 2 writes to *Y. This is the two-step write pattern.\"}],\"verification_result\":{\"executed\":false,\"poc_path\":\"/work/test/poc-BUG-001.py\",\"written_value\":\"\",\"read_value\":\"\",\"fault_address\":\"\",\"return_code\":0,\"details\":\"Not dynamically verified as full two-step write. Step 1 is verified (PRIM-002 proves __dso_handle can be overwritten). Step 2 is structurally sound (msg[-11] re-reads current __dso_handle value, confirmed by crash). Full verification requires: (1) PIE base leak to construct valid Y, (2) Y must point to readable memory to avoid post-write crash. Marked THEORETICAL because the two-step structure is proven but the complete ARB_WRITE (two different Y values tested) is not dynamically verified.\"},\"confidence\":\"MEDIUM\",\"notes\":\"THEORETICAL because: (1) Step 1 write is dynamically verified (PRIM-002), (2) msg[-11] re-read behavior is dynamically verified (crash proves it), (3) but complete two-step sequence (Step 1 + Step 2 without crash) is not dynamically verified. The main barrier is that Step 1 crashes unless Y+read_return is readable, which requires PIE base knowledge. The two-step write structure is sound: __dso_handle is self-referencing, msg[-11] re-reads current value, and msg_size[-11] remains valid across calls. This is classified as INDIRECT because it requires an intermediate step (overwriting the pointer before writing through it).\"}],\"non_primitives\":[{\"primitive_id\":\"NP-001\",\"candidate_type\":\"ARB_READ\",\"source_bug\":\"BUG-001\",\"reason\":\"read_cookie with negative index can only read from fixed FILE pointers (stderr/stdin/stdout) at fixed negative indices (-4/-6/-8). The read target is NOT attacker-controlled - it is determined by which BSS global the negative index aliases. printf %s also limits the read to bytes before the first null. This does not meet ARB_READ criteria (target address must be attacker-controlled). Classified as INFO_LEAK instead.\"},{\"primitive_id\":\"NP-002\",\"candidate_type\":\"ARB_WRITE (direct)\",\"source_bug\":\"BUG-001\",\"reason\":\"edit_cookie with negative index -4/-6/-8 writes to FILE structures (stderr/stdin/stdout), but the write target is a FIXED address (the FILE structure pointed to by the BSS FILE pointer). The write fails because msg_size at those indices is 0 (underflow to 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF, read returns -1). Even if it succeeded, the target would be fixed, not attacker-controlled. Direct ARB_WRITE does not exist; only the two-step indirect write (PRIM-003) can achieve ARB_WRITE.\"}],\"unresolved\":[{\"description\":\"PRIM-003 (ARB_WRITE via two-step) not fully dynamically verified\",\"reason\":\"Full two-step write requires: (1) PIE base leak to construct valid target Y, (2) Y must point to readable memory to avoid post-write crash in Step 1, (3) two different Y values must be tested to prove address controllability.\",\"required_next_step\":\"S4 can use PRIM-001 (INFO_LEAK) or other leaks to obtain PIE base, then construct valid Y addresses in BSS/.data segment (readable+writable) to complete the two-step write verification.\"},{\"description\":\"CET (IBT/SHSTK) status unknown\",\"reason\":\"checksec does not report CET flags. If CET is enabled, indirect branch tracking and shadow stack may affect control flow hijacking (S4 concern, not S3 primitive concern).\",\"required_next_step\":\"Runtime check via /proc/cpuinfo or arch_prctl in S4.\"}]}],\"target_bug\":\"BUG-001\",\"bug_reports\":[],\"impact_reports\":[],\"strategy_reports\":[],\"final_exploit_path\":\"\",\"final_report\":{}}",
